// The menus' strings, in English: each T(ID, "text") is tr::ID in the code (src/host/text.h). Every language has its
// own file (ko.inc, ja.inc, ...) with the same IDs; tools/langtest checks them (docs/i18n-design.md: how to add one).
// Whole sentences: what changes in one is a {name}, filled in by the code, and a translation puts it where its
// language does. UTF-8 (\xC2\xB7 a middle dot, \xE2\x80\x93 an en dash, \xE2\x80\x94 an em dash, \xC2\xA0 a space
// that doesn't break). Comments say where each is shown, and how much room there is where it's tight.
// Never translated: the game's own text (the ROM's), players' and rooms' names, codes, addresses, key and button
// names as they're printed (Enter, Esc, A, B, LB, Start), the games' names, "VS".

